\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {A.4}{\ignorespaces Gradient descent on $f = \tfrac  12(x_1^2 + 10x_2^2)$ from $(9, 2)$ (\cref  {ex:appB-gd}). The ellipses are level sets. The small step $\alpha = 0.05$ (blue) reaches the valley floor at once and then advances by only $5\,\%$ per step; the larger step $\alpha = 0.18$ (orange) zigzags across the valley and gets much closer to the minimum in the same $20$ steps. Any $\alpha > 0.2$ diverges.}}{25}{figure.caption.12}\protected@file@percent }
